# Rust
/target
**/*.rs.bk
# Cargo.lock is committed on purpose: this workspace builds binaries, so the
# resolved dependency set is part of the build. Leaving it out let a transitive
# release decide whether CI compiled, which is how a sqlx 0.7.4 / newer-rustc
# incompatibility first surfaced as a red build instead of a reproducible one.

# Node / Frontend
node_modules/
.nuxt/
.output/
dist/
.pnpm-store/
*.log
.DS_Store

# Env
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# Build
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll

